# Database safety

- Use read replicas / read-only roles for diagnosis; set statement timeouts.
- Require a transaction, bounded WHERE clause, dry-run/count query, and rollback plan for writes.
- Split migration work into plan_ / validate_ / apply_ / rollback_ tools.
- Reject long exclusive locks without an approval-gated window.
- Require backup/restore evidence before recommending production apply.
- Never expose superuser/owner credentials to the agent.
- Sanitize tenant IDs in generated tests; fail closed on cross-tenant access.
- Redact sampled row payloads; prefer EXPLAIN plans and metadata.
